<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Thanks F1RMB, I will flash the firmware. If it works I'll change the thread to solved. I'm just getting a firmware file too large error to work out first.</div></blockquote>I don't know which CPS version your using, or the firmware file you're trying to flash.<br>This error message appears when the selected file a not really an expected OpenGD77 firmware, as the firmware file has a size limit.<br>The MD-760 is a GD-77.</div></blockquote>Hi F1RMB, I was following the instructions by yours truly in this forum to ensure it was the latest files. The issue was me not reading past step 10 clearly and using the incorrect .bin file. I learnt the hard way it must be the open gd77 .bin file! As you also mentioned, upgrading the firmware (it was indeed very old, 2020) fixed the issue with the CPS software error. I will change the status to solved and hope this may assist others.</div></blockquote>Nice you solved the problem.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Sun Feb 23, 2025 11:35 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
